 by['fd:shut'].to); eq('blocked', by['fd:shut'].refused)\n    eq(nil, by.tonumber.to); eq(nil, by.tonumber.refused)\nend)"}}},{"bytes":733,"decided_by":"tactic","id":"1791229834.138402-edit","decisions":[],"verb":"edit","invocation":{"touched":["lua/cartograph/cache.lua"],"verb":"edit","args":{"file":"lua/cartograph/cache.lua","before":"M.VERSION = 215 -- v215: THREE RESOLUTION FIXES, ONE BUMP (the cache holds linked graphs; 65bb8cc and bc7560c shipped without moving it): a rebound parameter is no param write (CART-1484, the `pw` fact); a same-file name defined several times is bound by LEXICAL scope (CART-1059, Lua samefile 670 -> 33); a bare Lua call binds bare names only and a multi-assignment pairs name i with value i (CART-1487/1488: 714 bare calls had been linked to a wrong qualified def)","after":"M.VERSION = 216 -- v216: A LUA METHOD CALL IS NEVER LINKED TO A PLAIN FUNCTION (CART-1491): `x:f()` passes x as self, so a name-only resolution to `M.f(...)` / a local `f` is vetoed to a `blocked` refusal (1,053 such links on lua/: tree:root -> M.root, timer:is_closing -> a local)\n-- v215: THREE RESOLUTION FIXES, ONE BUMP (the cache holds linked graphs; 65bb8cc and bc7560c shipped without moving it): a rebound parameter is no param write (CART-1484, the `pw` fact); a same-file name defined several times is bound by LEXICAL scope (CART-1059, Lua samefile 670 -> 33); a bare Lua call binds bare names only and a multi-assignment pairs name i with value i (CART-1487/1488: 714 bare calls had been linked to a wrong qualified def)"}}},{"bytes":1895,"decided_by":"tactic","id":"1791230064.916962-edit","decisions":[],"verb":"edit","invocation":{"touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"],"verb":"edit","args":{"file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md","before":" Not yet: a nested field through an alias (`lib.FAMILIES.tonumber`) is refused `blocked` (CART-1489); other languages without an implicit receiver (python, js, go, rust) are not flag